{
  "question": "What is the NYC M/WBE noncompetitive small purchase limit?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "The NYC M/WBE noncompetitive small purchase limit is $1,500,000. This rule is established by the New York City Charter and implemented through NYC PPB Rules, which allow agencies to make procurements from certified M/WBE vendors without a formal competitive process up to this amount.",
